estarted, boot ID changed, and worker log continued appending after restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Created system user inventory-worker (nologin shell) and directory /var/lib/inventory owned by it, mode 750\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh: a long-running loop that appends timestamped ticks to /var/lib/inventory/worker.log every 10s\",\"Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service running as inventory-worker with NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=strict, ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory, plus additional hardening (PrivateTmp, ProtectHome, PrivateDevices, CapabilityBoundingSet=, SystemCallFilter=@system-service, etc.)\",\"Enabled and started the service; verified Active: running, NoNewPrivs=1 in /proc/PID/status\",\"Verified confinement: write to /etc/should-fail as inventory-worker returned Permission denied (exit=1); write to /var/lib/inventory/should-work succeeded (exit=0); cleaned up the test file\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime, service active state, growing log\",\"Triggered systemctl reboot on node1 (self-scheduled after 2s so the exec ack returned first)\",\"Polled node1 until reachable; observed connection timeout/reset during reboot, then successful reconnection\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed from 4a743885-c59f-43ee-afde-ef96f7bea723 to a8869031-5516-4307-bbae-318914d30051 and uptime reset, proving an actual restart\",\"Confirmed post-restart recovery: service enabled+active with new PID, worker.log continued appending new ticks (pre-restart entries preserved)\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Service inventory-worker created, managed by systemd, running as long-lived background worker\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-98e455488aa84427\",\"cmd-9c0a2b95e55e409d\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl enable --now succeeded; status shows Active: running with worker process and sleep child; is-enabled/is-active both confirm managed service state\"},{\"requirement\":\"Confined to write only inside /var/lib/inventory\",\"command_ids\":[